.TH SIMRV 1 "October 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv \- explainable RISC-V architectural simulator and TUI workbench
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv
simulates RV32 and RV64 RISC-V guests.  It provides a high-speed functional engine,
detailed and cycle-accurate pipeline models, an interactive terminal workbench, a
GDB Remote Serial Protocol server, and headless automation outputs.
.PP
The normal release binary is RV64-capable and can execute both RV64 and RV32 guests.
Native RV32 builds are intended for strict-width verification.  When standard input
is a terminal, SimRV starts the TUI unless an explicit headless mode is selected.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cli
Force headless command-line execution.  This is recommended for scripts, CI, and
profiling.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-tui
Force the interactive terminal workbench.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-baremetal
Load and execute a bare-metal application (the default execution personality).
.TP
.B \-\-os
Boot an operating-system image using the supplied firmware, disk, and device tree.
.TP
.B \-\-mode=\fImode\fR
Select the execution engine: \fBfast\fR, \fBdetailed\fR, or
\fBcycle-accurate\fR.  Cycle-accurate mode exposes pipeline and timing state.
.TP
.B \-R, \-\-realtime
Throttle execution to host real time.  Use \fB\-\-no-realtime\fR to disable
real-time pacing explicitly.
.SH IMAGE AND MEMORY OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-image, \-\-memory \fIfile\fR
Load an ELF or raw binary image into guest memory.
.TP
.B \-\-pc, \-\-start-pc \fIaddress\fR
Set the initial program counter.  The default is \fB0x80000000\fR.
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-disk, \-\-rootfs \fIfile\fR
Attach a VirtIO block disk or root filesystem image.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fdt, \-\-dtb \fIfile\fR
Load a device-tree blob for operating-system boot.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-tohost-addr \fIaddress\fR
Set the guest \fBtohost\fR termination address.
.TP
.B \-\-dram-size, \-\-ram-size \fIsize\fR
Set guest DRAM size.  Numeric values accept \fBk\fR, \fBM\fR, and \fBG\fR
suffixes; the default is 256 MiB for bare metal and 1 GiB for Linux.
.SH ARCHITECTURE AND PLATFORM
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-harts, \-\-smp \fIn\fR
Configure one to sixteen simulated harts.
.TP
.B \-\-smp-quantum=\fIn\fR
Set the round-robin SMP scheduling quantum in cycles.
.TP
.B \-\-smp-multithreaded
Run SMP simulation workers on multiple host threads.
.TP
.B \-\-isa=\fIpreset\fR
Select the guest ISA preset: \fBrv32i\fR, \fBrv32imac\fR, \fBrv32gc\fR,
\fBrv32gcbv\fR, \fBrv64i\fR, \fBrv64imac\fR, \fBrv64gc\fR, or \fBrv64gcbv\fR,
subject to the host build's capabilities.
.TP
.B \-\-vlen=\fIbits\fR
Set the vector register length from 128 through 1024 bits.
.TP
.B \-\-soc=\fIpreset\fR
Select a complete SoC platform: \fBvirt-pcie\fR, \fBvirt-mmio\fR, or \fBrvcomp\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-net=\fIbackend\fR
Select the VirtIO network backend: \fBuser\fR, \fBtap\fR, \fBsocket\fR, or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dump-soc-manifest=\fIpreset\fR [\fIfile\fR]
Write the normalized SoC registry as JSON.
.SH EXECUTION AND PIPELINE
.TP
.B \-s, \-e, \-\-steps \fIn\fR
Stop after \fIn\fR instructions have retired across all harts.
.TP
.B \-t, \-l, \-\-timer \fIn\fR
Enable a CLINT timer interrupt after \fIn\fR cycles.
.TP
.B \-\-pipeline=\fItype\fR
Select the cycle-accurate pipeline target: \fB3stage\fR or \fB5stage\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no-forwarding
Disable operand forwarding in the cycle-accurate pipeline.
.TP
.B \-\-bpred=\fItype\fR
Select the branch predictor: \fBnone\fR, \fBstatic\fR, \fBbimodal\fR,
\fBgshare\fR, or \fBtournament\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-bht-size=\fIn\fR, \-\-btb-size=\fIn\fR, \-\-ras-size=\fIn\fR
Configure branch-history, branch-target-buffer, and return-address-stack sizes.
.TP
.B \-\-cpu-preset=\fIpreset\fR
Select a built-in CPU model (\fBtiny\fR, \fBbalanced\fR, or \fBperformance\fR)
or load a model configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-cpu-config=\fIfile\fR
Load a microarchitectural latency configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-dump-cpu-model=\fImodel\fR [\fIfile\fR]
Export a normalized CPU model configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-scaffold-cpu-model [\fIfile\fR]
Generate a starter CPU model configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-validate-cpu-config=\fIfile\fR
Validate and lint a CPU model configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-cfu-plugin=\fIfile.so\fR
Load a dynamic custom function-unit plugin.
.SH LOGGING, TRACING, AND PROFILING
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress startup logs and use warning-level logging.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable debug-level diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-\-log-level=\fIlevel\fR
Set the console log level to \fBtrace\fR, \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR,
\fBwarn\fR, \fBerror\fR, or \fBoff\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-log-file=\fIfile\fR
Mirror timestamped console log messages to a file.
.TP
.B \-\-summary=\fIfile.json\fR
Write a machine-readable execution summary when the run exits.
.TP
.B \-\-events=\fIfile.jsonl\fR
Write newline-delimited lifecycle events while the run progresses.
.TP
.B \-\-instmix
Write an instruction-mix report to \fBtrace/instmix.txt\fR on exit.
.TP
.B \-\-arch-trace=\fIfile.jsonl\fR
Write a JSONL architectural retirement trace in detailed mode.
.TP
.B \-\-trace-level=\fI0\-4\fR
Limit architectural event detail: level 1 devices and traps, level 2 calls and returns, level 3
retirement, and level 4 detailed state.
.TP
.B \-\-trace
Write an aligned architectural trace to \fBtrace/trace.txt\fR.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-trace-range \fIbegin end\fR
Capture a trace for an inclusive execution range.
.TP
.B \-\-trace-pc-period=\fIn\fR
Sample the program counter every \fIn\fR steps into \fBtrace/tracepc.txt\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-trace-bpred
Record branch-prediction decisions.
.TP
.B \-\-log-mmio
Record MMIO transactions in \fBtrace/dlog.txt\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-trap-log=\fIfile\fR
Write architectural trap and SBI events to a file.
.TP
.B \-I, \-\-dump-init=\fIcycle\fR
Dump initial architectural memory and TLB state at a selected cycle.
.SH DEBUGGING AND CHECKPOINTS
.TP
.B \-\-gdb
Start the GDB Remote Serial Protocol server in CLI mode.  The target starts
paused and accepts connections from a RISC-V GDB client.
.TP
.B \-\-gdb-port=\fIport\fR
Listen on the specified TCP port.  Port 1234 is the default; port 0 selects
an ephemeral port and reports the selected port on standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-save-checkpoint=\fIfile\fR
Save architectural state when the run exits.
.TP
.B \-\-load-checkpoint=\fIfile\fR
Resume from an architectural checkpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-lockstep
Enable Spike lockstep verification.  GDB and lockstep are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.B \-\-spike-bin=\fIfile\fR
Select the Spike executable used for lockstep verification.
.TP
.B \-\-spike-elf=\fIfile\fR
Select the Spike-side ELF image used for lockstep verification.
.SH TUI WORKBENCH
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume execution.  While running, input is routed to the guest terminal.
.TP
.B n, F3
Step one machine cycle across all harts.
.TP
.B r
Run continuously.
.TP
.B Tab
Cycle the active inspector page.
.TP
.B q
Quit the simulator.
.PP
The TUI provides register, cache, TLB, pipeline, hazard, bus, I/O, performance,
trace, and instruction-explanation views.  Press \fB?\fR for in-application
keybinding and glossary help.
.SH INFORMATION AND DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the simulator version and target architecture.
.TP
.B \-\-isa-info
Print the qualified ISA and frontend capabilities.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Diagnose terminal, runtime, and release-environment issues.
.TP
.B \-\-explain-inst=\fIhex\fR
Disassemble and explain a 32-bit instruction encoding.
.TP
.B \-\-license
Display the MIT license and copyright notice.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print the complete command-line help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Bare-metal ELF
.EX
simrv --cli --baremetal -m hello.elf --isa rv64gc
.EE
.TP
.B Bounded profiling
.EX
simrv --cli -m hello.elf --steps 1000000 \\
  --summary run/summary.json --events run/events.jsonl --instmix
.EE
.TP
.B Cycle-accurate pipeline
.EX
simrv --cli -m hello.elf --mode cycle-accurate --pipeline 5stage
.EE
.TP
.B GDB debugging
.EX
simrv --gdb --gdb-port 1234 -m hello.elf --isa rv64gc
riscv64-unknown-elf-gdb hello.elf -ex 'target remote :1234'
.EE
.TP
.B Linux boot
.EX
simrv --cli --os -m fw_payload.bin -D root.img -f devicetree.dtb
.EE
.SH OUTPUT FILES
.TP
.B trace/
Default directory for architectural, PC, branch-prediction, MMIO, and
instruction-mix reports.
.TP
.B \-\-summary and \-\-events outputs
Explicit paths supplied by the caller.  Standard output remains available for
guest UART output; these options reject \fB-\fR as a destination.
.TP
.B /usr/share/SimRV/SimRVBuildMetadata.json
Installed build provenance containing the version, Git revision, target XLEN,
compiler, generator, and host information.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The guest completed normally or an informational command succeeded.
.TP
.B non-zero
Argument parsing, image loading, simulation, guest termination, or output
generation failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/simrv
The installed simulator executable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/simrv.1
This manual page.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/SimRV/USER_GUIDE.md
The complete user guide.
.TP
.I /usr/share/SimRV/SimRVBuildMetadata.json
Installed build provenance manifest.
